    "question": {
      ":question/id": "837b59b6-3b69-5ca7-b06a-a1bbfd1343c2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x-225^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter exact coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\sin(x-225^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-225^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 225^\\circ-\\cos x\\sin 225^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe plus sign outside the second blank is supplied. The entries are $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, respectively.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "db6b0ded-93d6-53fd-bf59-194023a309a1",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
